Independently authored. Its look and construction grew out of the author's earlier Measured
Light holograms; no code, fonts, shaders or assets from that work are included. Its working method is
inspired by Anatomy (github.com/wheresryan22/anatomy, MIT): no Anatomy code, assets or text
are included.

Third-party software: none is bundled. The toolkit uses the Python standard library only;
the viewer is plain WebGL2 and uses system fonts. Optional programs it can call when they
are already installed: a Chromium-family browser (review captures) and ffmpeg (video). Each
keeps its own licence and is never downloaded or installed by this toolkit.

Example artwork (construct_hologram/examples/v2/assets) is synthetic, generated by png.py, and
labelled as generated decoration. No authentic artwork, private data, credentials or model
weights are included.

Example constructs (examples/): scenes written by AI models (Claude Opus 5.5, GPT-6.1 Sol, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash)
with Construct, with hero images and animations rendered by Construct's own viewer. Those of real
things are independent reconstructions from public references (KESTREL is an invented design, and
SERUM 2 / 61 an unaffiliated concept designed from a public manual); the scenes cite their references
by URL and include no reference photograph, apart from the two worlds below. Product, vehicle and place names
belong to their owners, and no endorsement is implied.

The two worlds made from one picture each include that picture as reference.jpg. Rain Harbour's
(examples/worlds/rain-harbour/) is a concept picture made by the author and is Apache-2.0 with the rest.
